# Embedded Systems Escape Room Station

Developed a complete embedded systems station as part of an escape room scenario in an
Embedded Systems Architecture course. The project was implemented across multiple milestones,
covering microcontroller setup, hardware fabrication, system modeling, and full software–hardware
integration.

The system is built around an RP2040-based microcontroller and implements structured embedded
control logic using the Pico SDK. Custom drivers were developed for sensors and actuators following
best practices and proper abstraction layers. The station logic is governed by a state-based model
supporting concurrency, hierarchy, and robust error handling.

The final implementation integrates all sensors and actuators into a fully functional physical
station, ensuring reliable real-time behavior, correct timing, and stable operation according to
the escape room scenario. The project includes complete hardware enclosure design, organized
wiring, calibrated components, and safe power distribution suitable for repeated demonstrations.

